Package: csmGmmCorr
Type: Package
Title: Correlated Conditionally Symmetric Multidimensional Gaussian Mixtures
    for Composite Null Testing
Version: 1.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Z.", "Liu", email = "zliu20@mdanderson.org", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ryan", "Sun", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Author of the csmGmm method and package on which this package builds"))
Description: Fits a correlated conditionally symmetric multidimensional
    Gaussian mixture for composite-null testing when several statistics from
    the same feature are correlated. The model retains support-specific
    weights and magnitude components, a common within-feature correlation
    matrix, and a coordinatewise magnitude-ordering restriction. A single fit
    supports pleiotropy, same-sign replication, and mediation targets for any
    threshold. Estimation uses constrained expectation conditional
    maximization from multiple starts. Local false discovery rates are
    converted to discoveries by the Sun and Cai step-up rule. The package
    extends the conditionally symmetric mixture framework of Sun, McCaw, and
    Lin (2025) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2024.2422124>. Optional tools impose a
    specified monotone ordering and diagnose extrapolation.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/ZLiu20/csmGmmCorr
BugReports: https://github.com/ZLiu20/csmGmmCorr/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats
NeedsCompilation: yes
